    "text": "Excellent! All refactoring is complete and tested. Here's a summary of what was accomplished:\n\n## Refactoring Summary\n\n### 1. \u2705 Removed Duplicated Code in Tests 2-3\nCreated helper method `assertSalesForCustomer:includingCount:ofCombo:` to eliminate the repeated assertion pattern.\n\n### 2. \u2705 Removed Duplicated Code in Tests 9-14  \nCreated two helper methods:\n- `registerSales:toCustomer:` - registers multiple combos at once\n- `assertRewardFor:hasQuantity:isForCombo:atPrice:` - asserts all reward properties\n\nThis reduced 6 near-identical tests from ~50 lines to ~5 lines each.\n\n### 3. \u2705 Replaced `if`s with Polymorphism\n\n**Product Polymorphism:**\n- Created `CoffeeShopProduct` hierarchy with `Combo1Product` and `Combo2Product` subclasses\n- Each product encapsulates its volume and price\n\n**Customer Polymorphism:**\n- Created `GoldCustomer`, `SilverCustomer`, `NormalCustomer` subclasses with polymorphic reward pricing\n- Updated factory method to return appropriate subclass\n- Updated reward rules to use `rewardPriceForCombo1` and `rewardPriceFor:` methods\n\nAll 14 tests pass, and the image has been saved. The polymorphic design eliminates all conditional logic for customer types and products\u2014responsibility is now properly distributed across the type hierarchy."
